    "title": {
      "en": "Corncrake or Quail?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Both call from the grass at night. The Corncrake gives a dry, rasping 'crex-crex', two notes with a pause, like a comb across a matchbox. The Quail gives a short, liquid 'whit, whit-whit', with three notes, like “wet-my-lips”. The Corncrake is in damp hay meadows, the Quail in crops."
    }
